# promise: #691
# With the sidebar hidden and the toolbar too, the sidebar that slides out at the window's edge stays
# out while Arc's address panel hangs from its address, wherever the pointer goes, as in Arc 1.174.1.
# A click on the sidebar's empty space closes the panel; the sidebar is then free to go as the pointer
# says. Until 0.1.54 the sidebar slid away under the open panel, and a click on its empty space left
# the panel open: the sidebar's panel takes the keys only when a click needs them, so the bar never
# lost them. The pointer leaving is cra://debug?floatingSidebar=pointerAway, what the poll would do.
budget rss=800 stalls50=20
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false}
cra://debug?windowSize=1200x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=panel
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1
cra://action/toggleSidebar
wait 1
cra://debug?floatingSidebar=hold
wait 1
cra://debug?urlFieldEdit=click
expect-log url field click: not editing, command bar open, panel compact
cra://debug?floatingSidebar=release
cra://debug?floatingSidebar=pointerAway
wait 1
cra://debug?floatingSidebar=state:panel
expect-log floating sidebar panel: out$

# A click on the sidebar's empty space, below its tab.
cra://debug?clickAt=120,600&target=floating
wait 1
cra://debug?urlFieldEdit=state
expect-log url field state: not editing, command bar closed
cra://debug?floatingSidebar=pointerAway
wait 1
cra://debug?floatingSidebar=state:closed
expect-log floating sidebar closed: in$
